FUN_00420708: three matrices rebuilt in contiguous short[9] buffers (scattered-locals)

FUN_00420708 @0x420708 (align-to-direction matrix builder) constructs THREE 3x3 short
matrices on the stack: A @[ebp-0x44] (local_48..local_38), B @[ebp-0x84] (local_88..local_78),
C @[ebp-0x64] (local_68..local_58), then computes B = A x B (MulMatrix2) and out = B x C
(gte_MulMatrix0, out=param_1). Ghidra split every element into its own 2-byte local; passing
&local_88 etc. as matrix pointers relies on a stack layout the compiler does not guarantee.
Element mapping recovered by ebp-offset (local_NN <-> ebp-(NN-4)): A[0..1] are the two halves
of the uint local_48 (code writes the pair via a 32-bit store then masks & 0xffff -> A[1]=0).
Same scattered-locals class as MATRIXLOCALS RotMatrixZ / patch 330.

